{"subject":"golang","time":"2023-08-08T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.21.0"},"statement":"The standard library includes the packages slices, maps and cmp, providing generic functions over slices and maps and a generic ordering constraint cmp.Ordered.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.21","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2023-08-08T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.21.0"},"statement":"The standard library includes log/slog, a structured logging package with levels, key-value attributes and pluggable handlers.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.21","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2023-08-08T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.21.0"},"statement":"A go.mod file may contain a toolchain directive, and the go command automatically downloads and runs a newer Go toolchain when the go or toolchain line requires one (forward compatibility).","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.21","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2024-02-06T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.22.0"},"statement":"Each iteration of a for loop creates new loop variables, so closures and goroutines started in the loop body capture a per-iteration variable rather than one variable shared across iterations.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.22","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2024-02-06T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.22.0"},"statement":"A for-range loop may range over an integer n, iterating from 0 to n-1.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.22","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2024-02-06T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.22.0"},"statement":"The standard library includes math/rand/v2, which uses the ChaCha8 and PCG generators, drops the top-level Seed function, and provides generic helpers such as rand.N.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.22","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2024-02-06T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.22.0"},"statement":"net/http.ServeMux patterns may begin with an HTTP method and may contain wildcards such as {id} and {path...}, with values retrieved via Request.PathValue.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.22","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2024-08-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.23.0"},"statement":"A for-range loop may range over iterator functions of the forms func(yield func() bool), func(yield func(K) bool) and func(yield func(K, V) bool), and the iter package defines the Seq and Seq2 iterator types.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.23","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2024-08-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.23.0"},"statement":"The slices and maps packages provide iterator-based functions such as slices.All, slices.Values, slices.Collect, slices.Sorted, maps.Keys and maps.Values, where maps.Keys and maps.Values return iterators rather than slices.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.23","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2024-08-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.23.0"},"statement":"The standard library includes the unique package, which canonicalises (interns) comparable values via unique.Make and unique.Handle.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.23","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2024-08-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.23.0"},"statement":"For programs whose go.mod declares go 1.23 or later, timers and tickers created by the time package are garbage collected when unreferenced even if not stopped, and their channels are unbuffered so Stop and Reset guarantee no stale values are received.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.23","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2025-02-11T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.24.0"},"statement":"Generic type aliases are fully supported: a type alias may be parameterised like a defined type.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.24","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2025-02-11T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.24.0"},"statement":"A go.mod file may declare tool dependencies with the tool directive, go get -tool adds them, and go tool <name> runs them, replacing the tools.go blank-import convention.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.24","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2025-02-11T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.24.0"},"statement":"Benchmarks may use the testing.B.Loop method (for b.Loop() { ... }) instead of a loop over b.N; it handles timing and prevents the compiler from optimising away the body.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.24","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2025-02-11T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.24.0"},"statement":"The os package provides os.Root, which performs filesystem operations confined to a directory and rejects paths that escape it via .. or symbolic links.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.24","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2025-02-11T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.24.0"},"statement":"The standard library includes the weak package providing weak pointers (weak.Pointer), and the crypto/mlkem package implementing the ML-KEM post-quantum key encapsulation mechanism.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.24","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2025-02-11T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.24.0"},"statement":"encoding/json struct tags support the omitzero option, which omits a field when its value is the zero value for its type or when its IsZero method reports true.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.24","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2025-08-12T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.25.0"},"statement":"The language specification no longer uses the notion of core types; the rules formerly stated in terms of core types are expressed with dedicated prose. This does not change which programs are valid.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.25","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2025-08-12T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.25.0"},"statement":"The testing/synctest package is generally available, providing synctest.Test to run concurrent code in an isolated bubble with a fake clock and synctest.Wait to wait for goroutines in the bubble to block.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.25","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2025-08-12T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.25.0"},"statement":"An experimental encoding/json/v2 package and a redesigned encoding/json/jsontext package are available when building with GOEXPERIMENT=jsonv2.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.25","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2025-08-12T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.25.0"},"statement":"On Linux the runtime's default GOMAXPROCS is container aware: it respects cgroup CPU bandwidth limits and is updated when the limit or the CPU affinity changes.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.25","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2026-02-10T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.26.0"},"statement":"The built-in function new accepts an expression operand, new(expr), allocating a new variable initialised to the value of the expression and returning a pointer to it.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.26","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2026-02-10T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.26.0"},"statement":"A generic type may refer to itself in its own type parameter list, so constraints such as type Adder[A Adder[A]] interface { Add(A) A } are permitted.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.26","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2026-02-10T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.26.0"},"statement":"The go fix command applies modernizers built on the go vet analysis framework that rewrite code to current language and library idioms, and supports //go:fix inline directives for API migration; its obsolete historical fixers were removed.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.26","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2026-02-10T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.26.0"},"statement":"go mod init writes a go directive one minor version below the running toolchain (a 1.N toolchain writes go 1.(N-1).0) so new modules stay compatible with supported Go releases.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.26","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2026-02-10T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.26.0"},"statement":"The cmd/doc command and go tool doc have been removed; go doc takes the same flags and arguments and replaces them.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.26","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2026-02-10T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.26.0"},"statement":"The Green Tea garbage collector is enabled by default; it can be disabled with GOEXPERIMENT=nogreenteagc at build time.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.26","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2026-02-10T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.26.0"},"statement":"On 64-bit platforms the runtime randomises the heap base address at startup; this can be disabled with GOEXPERIMENT=norandomizedheapbase64.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.26","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2026-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.27.0"},"statement":"A method declaration may declare its own type parameters (generic methods). Interface methods may not declare type parameters and cannot be implemented by generic methods.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.27","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2026-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.27.0"},"statement":"A key in a struct literal may be any valid field selector for the struct type, such as a promoted field, not only a top-level field name.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.27","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2026-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.27.0"},"statement":"Function type inference applies wherever a generic function is assigned to a variable of, or converted to, a matching function type.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.27","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2026-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.27.0"},"statement":"The go command no longer supports the bzr version control system and cannot fetch modules hosted on bzr servers.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.27","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2026-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.27.0"},"statement":"go test runs the stdversion vet check by default, reporting use of standard library symbols newer than the Go version in force for the file.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.27","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2026-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.27.0"},"statement":"The asynctimerchan GODEBUG setting has been removed; channels created by the time package are always unbuffered regardless of GODEBUG.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.27","by":"seed"}
{"subject":"golang","time":"2026-08-19T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.27.0"},"statement":"The runtime/pprof goroutineleak profile, which reports goroutines blocked on concurrency primitives that can never be unblocked, is generally available and served by net/http/pprof at /debug/pprof/goroutineleak.","source":"https://go.dev/doc/go1.27","by":"seed"}
